    "title": "The Stay-at-Home Surge: How Racine Residents Are Reimagining Friday Night Fun - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Racine County Eye Staff ,\n14 hours ago In Racine, Wisconsin, more people are staying in on Friday nights, but that doesn’t mean they’re doing less. Across the city, routines are changing as people turn toward hands-on hobbies, themed nights, and low-key activities at home. Instead of heading out, they’re creating their own version of a weekend, whether that’s setting up a movie marathon or hosting a small gathering with a twist. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
